# openOODA SIMD/FP Deep Audit

Logline: Static deep-audit of the IEEE-754 Float const-fold and SSE emit module, finding gaps the 8-case runtime smoke did not cover, ranked by severity.

Setup: oodac/oodac/x86_emit_float.oo (252), x86_emit_float_routine.oo (85), x86_ssa_emit_float.oo (129), x86_emit.oo (205 dispatcher, lines 35 and 192-198). All read on 2026-08-25. No .oo file was modified. Note: the brief named x86_emit_alu.oo (248) as the SIMD module; that file is the integer-const ALU, not the FP/SIMD module. The actual SIMD/Float module is the x86_emit_float family. The bg_d5646ea7 subagent was given the same wrong file reference.

Beats:
  1. Inventory the SIMD/FP fns across the three files.
  2. Build an edge case matrix: NaN, Inf, +/-0, subnormal, overflow, underflow, sci-notation, type coercion, division by zero, 32-bit truncation, stack overrun.
  3. Rank the top 10 gaps the smoke did not catch, with file:line evidence.
  4. Recommend fix order with one-line risk per gap.
  5. List the test cases to add, one per gap.

residual: AArch64 SIMD/FP module and std/arch_x86 codegen path stay later.

File: openOODA/audit/simd-deep.oot
Static analysis only. No .oo file was modified.

---

## 1. SIMD fn inventory

| # | fn name | what it does | current edge case handling | file:line |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `x86_float_scale` | Returns 1e6 fixed-point scale. | None. Constant. | `x86_emit_float.oo:17` |
| 2 | `x86_float_parse` | Parses `[+/-]whole[.frac][e[+/-]exp]` to scaled int. | Handles `-` prefix, `.frac`, `e/E` exponent, but bad char returns 0 silently. | `x86_emit_float.oo:19-64` |
| 3 | `x86_float_fmt` | Formats scaled int to `whole.frac` (max 6 frac, trailing zeros trimmed). | Negative: recurses with positive then prepends `-`. Cannot emit `-0.0` (v=0 fails `v<0`). | `x86_emit_float.oo:66-95` |
| 4 | `x86_float_op` | PLUS / MINUS / STAR / SLASH on scaled ints. | SLASH with b==0 calls eprintln + process_exit(1) (fail-closed). No overflow check on STAR product. | `x86_emit_float.oo:97-110` |
| 5 | `x86_float_fold_atom` | Reads one atom: FLOAT literal, `-FLOAT`, `-IDENT`, IDENT. | Negative literal in atom does NOT set the `neg_zero` flag. Returns the negated value only. | `x86_emit_float.oo:112-147` |
| 6 | `x86_match_float_test` | Dispatch gate: true if any `Float` token or `FLOAT` literal is present. | None. Pure predicate. | `x86_emit_float.oo:149-160` |
| 7 | `x86_collect_and_emit_float` | Main fold+emit pipeline. Walks tokens, collects `let X: Float = F;` then folds the println chain, emits `.rodata` + `main` + `_println_float` call. | Tracks `neg_zero` only on chain MINUS, not on negative-literal atoms. Returns false on un-foldable. | `x86_emit_float.oo:167-252` |
| 8 | `x86_emit_float_routine` | Emits AT&T body of `_println_float` (zero-libc). Uses SSE: `movq %xmm0,%rax`, `cvttsd2si`, `subsd`, `mulsd`, `addsd`. | Extracts sign bit to %r8. `cvttsd2si` is 32-bit. No NaN/Inf detect. Stack buffer is 64 bytes. | `x86_emit_float_routine.oo:12-84` |
| 9 | `x86_ssa_float_atom` | SSA atom reader: FLOAT literal or IDENT. | No MINUS-atom branch. No `neg_zero` tracking. | `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:16-23` |
| 10 | `parse_v` (SSA) | Parses `[+/-]whole[.frac]` to scaled int. | **No `e/E` exponent branch.** Bad char returns 0. | `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:25-37` |
| 11 | `fmt_v` (SSA) | Formats scaled int. | Identical to x86_float_fmt. Cannot emit `-0.0`. | `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:39-51` |
| 12 | `op_v` (SSA) | PLUS/MINUS/STAR/SLASH. | **SLASH with b==0 returns 0 silently** — diverges from non-SSA fail-closed. | `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:53-60` |
| 13 | `fold_v` (SSA) | Folds a chain of atoms. | Returns bad on first non-atom. No neg_zero tracking. | `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:62-80` |
| 14 | `x86_ssa_emit_float_routine_text` | Returns verbatim `_println_float` body as a string. | None. Text passthrough. | `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:82-84` |
| 15 | `x86_ssa_emit_float_op` | Emits one SSE op (PLUS/MINUS/STAR/SLASH/I2F/F2I) for a future runtime-Float path. | **Defined but never called** by `x86_ssa_emit_float_program` (dead code today). | `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:86-94` |
| 16 | `x86_ssa_emit_float_program` | SSA path: tokenize, fold, emit `.rodata` + `main` + call. | No `neg_zero` branch. Fails closed by returning `""` on un-foldable. | `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:96-129` |

Total SIMD/FP fns counted: **16** (4 parsing/fmt, 2 ops, 3 fold/atom, 3 emit, 4 dispatch/glue).

---

## 2. Edge case matrix

| edge case | which fns handle it | which fns miss it | severity |
|---|---|---|---|
| NaN literal in source | none — parser rejects `NaN` token (b<48 falls through to `return 0`) | all of `x86_float_parse`, `parse_v` | high (silent 0) |
| +Inf / -Inf | none — same path as NaN | all parsers | high (silent 0) |
| Signed zero `-0.0` as atom | `x86_float_fold_atom` parses it but **does not set `neg_zero`**; `-0.0 - 0.0` happens to work because the chain MINUS sets the flag | `x86_collect_and_emit_float:200-218`, `x86_ssa_emit_float_program:117-128`, `x86_float_fmt`, `fmt_v` | high (smoke test 8 covers chain case only) |
| Underflow (subnormal / very small) | none — `v = v / 10` runs to 0 silently | `x86_float_parse:59`, `x86_float_op:107` | medium (precision loss) |
| Overflow (i64 wrap) | none — `v * 10` and `a * b` wrap silently | `x86_float_parse:60`, `x86_float_op:101` | high (wrong answer) |
| Subnormal IEEE-754 (1e-308) | none | `x86_float_op:107` (SLASH) | medium (returns 0) |
| Negative literals (`-1.5`, `-0.0`) | parsed; sign applied | `x86_collect_and_emit_float` does not propagate the atom's sign into `neg_zero` | high |
| Sci-notation (`1e10`, `1.5e-3`) | `x86_float_parse:46-61` parses it; smoke test 6 covers it | `parse_v` (SSA) at `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:25-37` **has no exponent branch** | high (SSA path silent 0) |
| Division by zero | `x86_float_op:102-107` calls eprintln + process_exit(1) (fail-closed); smoke test 7 covers it | `op_v` at `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:58` returns 0 silently | high (SSA silent) |
| Int to Float coercion | none — `x86_float_fold_atom:125-133` only does `-IDENT` for a Float-named ident; Int names are in `inames`, not `fnames` | all fold fns | medium (rejected as un-foldable) |
| Float to Int coercion | `x86_ssa_emit_float_op:92` defines F2I | never called (dead) | low (no path) |
| 32-bit truncation in `cvttsd2si` | none — for `|value| > 2^31` the runtime returns `0x80000000` and sign-extends to `-2147483648` | `x86_emit_float_routine.oo:28,33` | high (silent miscompile) |
| NaN / Inf in `cvttsd2si` | none — same `0x80000000` path | `x86_emit_float_routine.oo:12-84` | high (silent miscompile) |
| Stack overrun in `_println_float` | none — `sub $64, %rsp` then writes backwards from `rbp-1`; for `1e308` (~309 digits) the buffer is overrun | `x86_emit_float_routine.oo:18,40-58` | high (segfault) |
| Bad char in literal (`1.0a`) | `x86_float_parse:28,38,53` returns 0 | the const-fold treats the literal as 0.0 silently | medium |
| Duplicate Float name (`let a: Float = 1.0; let a: Float = 2.0`) | `x86_bind_idx` returns first match | `x86_collect_and_emit_float:184-198` accepts and shadows | low |
| Multi-println program | `x86_collect_and_emit_float:200` processes the first `println` and `return`s | second `println` is silently dropped | medium |
| Nested parens (`(a+b)*c`) | `x86_collect_and_emit_float:218` sets `bad=true` on `LPAREN` | fold path | low (refused, OK) |
| Trailing junk after exponent (`1e5abc`) | `x86_float_parse:51-55` returns 0 on non-digit inside exponent | silent 0 | medium |
| Bare `e` (`1.0e`) | `x86_float_parse:46-55` enters exponent, exp stays 0, returns 1.0 | silent 0-exp acceptance | low |

Edge cases counted: **20**.

---

## 3. Top 10 gaps

1. **`-0.0` as a negative literal atom loses its sign.** `x86_float_fold_atom` at `x86_emit_float.oo:117-134` computes `0 - x86_float_parse("0.0") = 0` and returns v=0; `x86_collect_and_emit_float` at `:200-218` only sets `neg_zero` on a chain MINUS op, never on an atom's sign. Smoke test 8 (`a - b` with a=b=0) happens to pass because the chain MINUS sets the flag, but `let b: Float = -0.0; println(b);` silently emits `.double 0.0`. **Severity: high** (smoke gives false confidence).

2. **SSA parser `parse_v` has no `e/E` exponent branch.** `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:25-37`. Any `1e10` literal routed through the SSA path parses as `1` (whole=1, no exponent), then folds to 1.0. Smoke test 6 covers the non-SSA path; the SSA path is un-tested. **Severity: high** (silent wrong answer).

3. **SSA divide-by-zero returns 0 silently.** `op_v` at `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:58`: `if b == 0 { return 0; }`. Diverges from non-SSA `x86_float_op:102-107` which fails-closed. If the SSA path is ever wired into the dispatcher, `0.0 / 0.0` will print `0.00` instead of refusing. **Severity: high** (fail-open).

4. **`x86_float_op` STAR product can overflow i64.** `x86_emit_float.oo:101`: `(a * b) / sc`. For a=1e9, b=1e9 (scaled), `a * b = 1e18` fits, but `a=1e10, b=1e10` gives 1e20 and wraps. No guard. **Severity: high** (wrong answer on edge inputs).

5. **`x86_float_parse` sci-notation positive-exponent loop has no overflow guard.** `x86_emit_float.oo:60`: `while k < exp { v = v * 10; k = k + 1; }`. For `1e15`, v starts at 1e6, becomes 1e21, overflows i64 to a small or negative value. The literal `1e15` then folds to garbage. **Severity: high** (silent wraparound).

6. **`cvttsd2si` 32-bit truncation in `_println_float` for `|value| > 2^31`.** `x86_emit_float_routine.oo:28,33`. Values like `5.0e9` round-trip to `-2147483648`. The signed-bit extraction at `:19-26` still works, but the integer-print loop at `:60-69` then prints a wrong sign-magnitude. **Severity: high** (silent miscompile).

7. **`_println_float` has no NaN/Inf detection.** `x86_emit_float_routine.oo:12-84`. The routine extracts the sign bit to %r8, runs `cvttsd2si` which on NaN/+Inf/-Inf returns `0x80000000`, then prints `-2147483648` or `0` depending on the sign bit. **Severity: high** (silent miscompile).

8. **`_println_float` stack overrun for very large integers.** `x86_emit_float_routine.oo:18,40-58`. `sub $64, %rsp` then writes backwards from `rbp-1`. A value with > 60 digits (e.g. `1e60` scaled) writes past the saved RBP and clobbers the return address. The fixed-point scale of 1e6 means folded values can reach `9.2e18` before i64 saturates — at most 19 integer digits, plus sign, dot, 2 frac, newline = 24 bytes, safe. But the `cvttsd2si` truncation at #6 produces the fixed 11-char "-2147483648" so this only matters for the rare path that does NOT use the const-fold and relies on runtime movsd. **Severity: medium** (bounds-check missing in the routine).

9. **`_println_float` no rounding mode for fractional part.** `x86_emit_float_routine.oo:31-37`. `addsd 0.5` then truncate = round-half-up. For `0.005` this rounds to `0.01`; for `0.0049999...` to `0.00`. Smoke test 5 (`0.1 + 0.2 = 0.30`) tolerates the precision, but the round-half-up vs IEEE-754 round-half-to-even mismatch is a real divergence. **Severity: low** (smoke accepts it).

10. **Bad char in float literal returns 0 silently.** `x86_emit_float.oo:28,38,53` returns 0 on any non-digit in whole/frac/exponent. The const-fold then treats `1.0a` as `0.0`, masking a typo. **Severity: medium** (silent wrong answer, no fail-closed).

Gaps counted: **10** (3 high-severity parser, 3 high-severity runtime, 2 medium, 2 low).

---

## 4. Recommended fix order

| order | gap | one-line fix | risk |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | #1 `-0.0` atom loses sign | In `x86_float_fold_atom:117-134`, return a third list element `1` when the source was `-0.0`; in `x86_collect_and_emit_float:203-218`, OR the atom's neg-flag into `neg_zero`. | low — adds a struct field to atom return, callers already list-shape-only. |
| 2 | #3 SSA divide-by-zero | Change `op_v` at `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:58` to call `eprintln` + `process_exit(1)` matching `x86_float_op:102-107`. | low — same fail-closed contract. |
| 3 | #2 SSA no-sci-notation | Copy the `e/E` branch from `x86_float_parse:46-61` into `parse_v` at `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:25-37`. | low — same scale, same overflow characteristics. |
| 4 | #5, #4 overflow guards | Add an i64-overflow check before each `v = v * 10` and `(a * b)` in `x86_float_parse:60` and `x86_float_op:101`; on overflow, fail-closed with `ERR float overflow`. | medium — needs a portable overflow check in openOODA; may not exist yet. |
| 5 | #6, #7 `cvttsd2si` 32-bit + NaN/Inf | Switch to `cvttsd2siq` (64-bit) in `x86_emit_float_routine.oo:28,33`; add an exponent-bit check (`and $0x7FF0000000000000, %rax; cmp $0x7FF0000000000000, %rax`) before the convert to refuse NaN/Inf. | medium — requires the host to accept the `q` suffix (it does on x86-64). |
| 6 | #8 stack overrun | Reserve more stack (`sub $512, %rsp`) or write a length-first pass; the const-fold removes most large values but a runtime path remains. | low. |
| 7 | #9 rounding mode | Replace the `addsd 0.5` with banker's rounding (compare `frac - floor(frac)`, pick nearest even) or accept the round-half-up as documented. | low. |
| 8 | #10 bad char | Change `return 0` to `eprintln` + `process_exit(1)` in `x86_float_parse:28,38,53`. | low. |

---

## 5. Test cases to add

| gap | test case (one-line) |
|---|---|
| #1 `-0.0` atom | `let b: Float = -0.0; println(b);` → must print `-0.00`. |
| #1 chain variant | `let a: Float = 0.0; let b: Float = -0.0; println(a + b);` → must print `-0.00`. |
| #2 SSA sci-notation | `let a: Float = 1e10; println(a);` routed through `emit-x86-ssa` → must print `10000000000.00`. |
| #3 SSA div-by-zero | `let a: Float = 0.0; let b: Float = 0.0; println(a / b);` via `emit-x86-ssa` → must refuse with `float not const-foldable`. |
| #4 STAR overflow | `let a: Float = 1e5; let b: Float = 1e5; println(a * b);` → must refuse (overflow) or print correct `10000000000.00`. |
| #5 sci overflow | `let a: Float = 1e15; println(a);` → must refuse or print `1000000000000000.00`; never wrap. |
| #6 32-bit truncation | `let a: Float = 5000000000.0; println(a);` (post fold, runtime path) → must print `5000000000.00`, not `-2147483648.00`. |
| #7 NaN/Inf input | Inject `0.0 / 0.0` into runtime path (today refuses at fold); add a `Float` source-level `nan` literal handler that refuses. |
| #8 stack overrun | Feed a runtime path with `1e60` and assert no segfault. |
| #9 rounding | `let a: Float = 0.005; println(a);` → must print `0.01` (round-half-up) or `0.00` (banker's), but be deterministic. |
| #10 bad char | `let a: Float = 1.0a; println(a);` → must refuse with `float not const-foldable: bad char in literal`, not silently print `0.00`. |

Test cases to add: **11** (one per gap plus a chain variant for #1).

---

## 6. Summary

* Brief misnamed the file: `x86_emit_alu.oo` is the integer ALU; the SIMD/FP module is `x86_emit_float.oo` + `x86_emit_float_routine.oo` + `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo`. bg_d5646ea7 should be redirected.
* 16 SIMD/FP fns inventoried across 3 files.
* 20 edge cases enumerated; 10 are un-handled today.
* 3 highest-priority gaps: #1 (`-0.0` atom sign loss — smoke green-by-accident), #3 (SSA divide-by-zero silent), #2 (SSA parser no sci-notation).
* Fix order targets the 3 high-severity silent-wrong-answer gaps first, then overflow guards, then the runtime `cvttsd2si` truncation class.
